Standards: SDD

Purpose:
  .sdd system standards — naming, levels, states, relations,
  conventions. These are the global rules that all .sdd files
  must follow.

Owns: ./

ReadOrder:
   1  @naming.sdd
   2  @levels.sdd
   3  @states.sdd
   4  @relations.sdd
   5  @conventions.sdd

Modes:
  PARSE   — parse and validate .sdd files
  VALIDATE — validate against schemas
  REBUILD — rebuild INDEX from entities

Rules:
  [ST1]  .sdd files are AI engineering knowledge, not documentation.
  [ST2]  Code is source-of-truth for implementation; .sdd is source-of-truth for engineering knowledge.
  [ST3]  docs/ is human explanation layer.
  [ST4]  DO NOT DUPLICATE KNOWLEDGE. REFERENCE IT.
  [ST5]  IDs are immutable; titles can change.
  [ST6]  INDEX files are derived metadata, not source of truth.
  [ST7]  Schema validation MUST run on every .sdd file load.
  [ST8]  Circular dependencies MUST be detected.
  [ST9]  Orphaned entities MUST be detected.
  [ST10] Duplicate IDs MUST be detected.
  [ST11] Stale references MUST be detected.
  [ST12] .sdd files MUST be created only for knowledge entities, not every code file.
  [ST13] Documentation level: none, summary, detailed, operational.
  [ST14] Diagrams are .mmd files, not images.
  [ST15] Context loading priority: L0-L6.

Entry:
  Read:
    INDEX.sdd

  Resolve:
    naming
    levels
    states
    relations
    conventions

Navigation:
  Standards: @standards/INDEX.sdd
  Naming: @standards/naming.sdd
  Levels: @standards/levels.sdd
  States: @standards/states.sdd
  Relations: @standards/relations.sdd
  Conventions: @standards/conventions.sdd

State: +
  